The Z-parameter matrix of a two-port network relates the port voltages and port currents as follows:
<br><br>$$\left[\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{V}_{1} \\
\mathrm{~V}_{2}
\end{array}\right]=\mathrm{Z}\left[\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{I}_{1} \\
\mathrm{I}_{2}
\end{array}\right]$$<br><br>
The Z-parameter matrix (with each entry in ohms) of the network shown below is __________. <br><img src="/question-images/ec/2025/ec-2025-a48445eb7c.webp"/><br>

detailed_solution.markdown:
$\Delta \rightarrow \mathrm{Y}$ conversion

( $\mathrm{Z} \rightarrow \mathrm{Z} / 3$ )

<img src="/question-images/ec/2025/ec-2025-4f2a32f3f0.webp"/>

For T-network, Z-parameters

$$\begin{aligned}

& {\left[\begin{array}{ll}

\mathrm{Z}_{11} & \mathrm{Z}_{12}

\mathrm{Z}_{21} & \mathrm{Z}_{22}

\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}

\frac{8}{3}+\frac{2}{3} & \frac{2}{3}

\frac{2}{3} & \frac{8}{3}+\frac{2}{3}

\end{array}\right]}

& {[\mathrm{Z}]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}

\frac{10}{3} & \frac{2}{3}

\frac{2}{3} & \frac{10}{3}

\end{array}\right]}

\end{aligned}$$

Therefore, the correct answer is **A**.

$$\begin{aligned}

\mathrm{Q} &=\iint 4|\mathrm{y}| \mathrm{dx} \mathrm{dy}=4 \iint 4 \mathrm{ydx} \mathrm{dy} \\

& =16 \int \mathrm{dx} \int \mathrm{ydy}=16[\mathrm{x}]_{0}^{2}\left[\frac{\mathrm{y}^{2}}{2}\right]_{0}^{2} \\

& =16 \times 2 \times \frac{2^{2}}{2}=16 \times 4=64 \mu \mathrm{C}

\end{aligned}$$

Therefore, the correct answer is **C**.
